Theorem~\ref{thm:cmean}
guarantees $m \in L^{2}(P_X)$, so the relevant approximation question is
whether $\{\varphi_j\}$ is dense in $L^{2}(P_X)$.

When
$P_{Y\mid X=x}$ is a point mass $P_X$-almost surely the aleatoric term
vanishes, $R^2(m)=1$, and deterministic modeling is fully adequate;
